==Overview==
<tabber> 
Unawakened=
{{#tag:tabber|Pros=
{{Overview|Pros|type=Unawakened
|'''General'''
* Good damage.
* Most moves have powerful knockbacks.
* All moves can [[Instinct/Break|break Instinct]].
* Very easy to use.

|'''[Z] Quake Punch'''
* Decent [[Area of Effect|AoE]]
* Quite wide hitbox compared to its visuals.

|'''[X] Quake Wave'''
* Good range.

|'''[C] Quake Erupt'''
* Decent [[Area of Effect|AoE]].

|'''[V] Dual Tsunami'''
* Extremely large [[Area of Effect|AoE]].
* Breaks Instinct no matter what.
* Very high damage.
* Tsunami are not bound to physics, and can be summoned at any height.
}}

{{!}}-{{!}}Cons=
{{Overview|Cons|type=Unawakened
|'''General'''
* No mobility.
* Long cooldown on all moves.
* Mostly close-ranged.
* Hard to use in [[Water]], unless the user has [[Shark]] V2 and above.
* Quake moves also shake the users’ screen while they're being used.
* Knockback makes it less viable in grinding.
* Moves have long delays, making the player vulnerable.

|'''[Z] Quake Punch'''
* Long start-up.
* Huge knockback.

|'''[X] Quake Wave'''
* The energy ball is slow.

|'''[C] Quake Erupt'''
* High knockback.

|'''[V] Dual Tsunami'''
* Can be easily dodged with any move that has vertical mobility.
* Needs to be close to a surface, so the move doesn't fail.
}}
}}

|-|Awakened=
{{#tag:tabber|Pros=
{{Overview|Pros|type=Awakened
|'''General'''
* Shorter cooldowns compared to its Unawakened version.
* All moves deal extreme damage, depleting opponent HP very quickly if not careful.
* All moves can [[Instinct/Break|break Instinct]], and cannot be instinct tricked.
* All moves have large hitboxes.

|'''[Z] Fatal Demolisher'''
* Gives damage immunity when the user hits a target.
* No endlag.
* Short cooldown.
* Strong hitscan.
* Perfect combo starter, ender, and extender.

|'''[X] Air Crusher'''
* Good [[Area of Effect|AoE]].
* Good range.
* Slightly stuns the opponent at the push.
* Extends roughly 30% farther than its visuals.
* Very high damage.

|'''[C] Spatial Shockwave'''
* Good [[Area of Effect|AoE]].
* Can be used as a counter move if the opponent comes too close to the user.
* Very high damage.

|'''[V] Seaquake'''
* High stun. (1.5 seconds), often ending fights once landed.
* Extremely high damage, with both the slam and tsunamis combined easily dealing over half a player's HP.
* The ground slam and the waves have an extremely wide hitbox.
* Can be used aerially, dragging opponents down with the user if near them.
* Good damage.
* Largest [[Area of Effect|AoE]] in the game.
}}

{{!}}-{{!}}Cons=
{{Overview|Cons|type=Awakened
|'''General'''
* No mobility.
* Hard to use in [[water]], unless the user has [[Shark]] V2 and above.
* All moves have decent or high knockback.

|'''[Z] Fatal Demolisher'''
* Single-target.
* Cannot hit [[Sea Beast]]s.

|'''[X] Air Crusher'''
* Unfairly forced end-lag. (About 0.5 seconds).
** If the user uses flashstep to avoid it, they will be teleported back.
* The energy ball is not very quick.

|'''[C] Spatial Shockwave'''
* Bad start-up.
* Vulnerable to counterattack if missed.
* As of recent updates. [[AoE]] is not considered very remarkable.

|'''[V] Seaquake'''
* Needs to be close to the ground.
* Tsunami can be easily dodged with a mobility move.
* Due to the heights battles take place at, the move often never gets to hit the floor on its own, requiring support via [[Sword]] or [[Flash Step]].
}}
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* Although Quake's awakened {{Ability|V|1}} has two extra tsunamis, they do less total damage than Quake's unawakened {{Ability|V}}. 
* Quake shares its price with [[Bisento]].

